# ── Screenwise environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a monorepo. Each workspace loads its OWN .env from its own folder -
# there is no single shared .env. Copy each example to a real .env beside it:
#
#   cp frontend/.env.example frontend/.env
#   cp backend/.env.example  backend/.env
#
# Then fill in the values. Every .env file is gitignored.
#
# frontend/.env
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL   Base URL of the backend API.
#                       Default: http://localhost:5000/api
#
# backend/.env
#   PORT                Port the API listens on. Default: 5000
#   MONGODB_URI         MongoDB connection string (local or Atlas).
#   JWT_SECRET          Long random string used to sign JWTs.
#                       node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#   RESEND_API_KEY      Email provider key, so the candidate-email composer
#   / SMTP_*            delivers for real. Left blank, messages are only
#                       logged by the server. backend/.env.example walks
#                       through both options.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
